	(text "Where V_{UVLO(R)} = 1.2V\n	  V_{OV(R)} = 1.2V\n	  R_{1} = 470K\n	  R_{2} = 100K\nUV: 3V = 1.2V x (470000 + 100000 + R_{3}) / (100000 + R_{3})\nR_{2} = 213,333\nOV: 4V = 1.2V x (470000 + 100000 + R_{3}) / (R_{3})\nR_{3} = 244,286\nSo, R_{3} = 240K"
